      "snippet": {
        "text": "Hypertension complicates approximately 9% of all pregnancies with preeclampsia-eclampsia (up to 4%) being a major cause of maternal and perinatal morbidity and mortality. In severe preeclampsia, uteroplacental perfusion is usually diminished and this results in increased IUGR incidence, fetal hypoxia and perinatal death. Conservative treatment is usually kept limited to those with biophysic profile of 4 and above, largest vertical amniotic sac of >2 or estimated ultrasonographic fetal weight above 5th percentile (1).",
