  "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abdominal_decompression",
  "title": "Abdominal decompression",
  "content": "Definition\n- Abdominal decompression: an obstetric procedure that applies intermittent negative pressure to a pregnant woman's abdomen.\n\nMain findings / conclusions\n- No benefits found in healthy pregnant women. (Cochrane review)\n- No effect on maternal blood pressure.\n- No effect on newborn condition or subsequent intellectual development.\n- Effects on pre-eclampsia, low birthweight and fetal distress during labour are unclear.\n\nProcedure parameters\n- Device: rigid covered dome placed around the abdomen.\n- Negative pressure: \u221250 to \u2212100 mmHg.\n- Timing: 15\u201330 seconds out of each minute for 30 minutes; frequency one to three times daily, or continuous during labour.\n\nOther use\n- Has been used to treat abdominal compartment syndrome (ACS), aiding patients with elevated intra-abdominal pressure (IAP) and organ dysfunction (retrospective study).\n\nRelated fields\n- Maternal-fetal medicine\n- Obstetrical nursing\n\nKey references\n1) Hofmeyr GJ, Kulier R (13 June 2012). \"Abdominal decompression in normal pregnancy.\" The Cochrane Database of Systematic Reviews (6) CD001062. doi:10.1002/14651858.CD001062.pub2. PMC7050618. PMID 22696321.\n\n2) Hofmeyr GJ (13 June 2012). \"Abdominal decompression for suspected fetal compromise/pre-eclampsia.\" The Cochrane Database of Systematic Reviews (6) CD000004. doi:10.1002/14651858.CD000004.pub2. PMC7061357. PMID 22696313.\n\n3) De Waele J; Desender L; De Laet I; Ceelen W; Pattyn P; Hoste E (2010). \"Abdominal decompression for abdominal compartment syndrome in critically ill patients: a retrospective study.\" Acta Clinica Belgica. 65(6): 399\u2013403. doi:10.1179/acb.2010.65.6.005. hdl:1854/LU-1112776. PMID 21268953. S2CID 6501463.",
